@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+title: Audio generation and video input
+---
+
+`POST /v1/audio/generate` uses the pinned Omni diffusion-audio contract. Its
+`audio_generation` task is distinct from `speech_generation` and Chat audio
+output. Configure `api_format: audio_generate`, a `vllm-omni` transport binding,
+and the actual model's `text` and `audio_generation` capabilities. The caller's
+prompt, format, speed, duration, start offset, negative prompt, guidance, steps,
+and seed survive routing. Unknown fields and invalid values fail at ingress.
+The locked backend does not implement SSE for this API; the router rejects it.
+Binary output and errors pass through without a Speech or Chat conversion.
+Prompt context bounds still apply; no text output-token reserve is invented.
+
+Chat Completions accepts `video_url: {url: ...}` content parts in user messages,
+using HTTP(S) URLs or base64 video data URLs. Video stays a separate neutral
+content kind and requires `video_input` on the selected model. The router does
+not fetch URLs or decode video frames. Mixed text, image, audio, and video input
+uses the combined model capability demand. A registered path or codec is not
+proof that a loaded model supports it; downstream release reports distinguish
+mock transport testing from actual model inference.
diff --git a/website/docs/api/native-chat-audio-output.md b/website/docs/api/native-chat-audio-output.md
