--- /dev/null
+++ b/website/docs/api/native-chat-audio-output.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# Native Chat mixed audio output
+
+The patch decodes `modalities: ["text", "audio"]` (or either modality) and
+`audio: {format, voice}` into `LLMRequest.ChatOutput`. The format accepts wav,
+mp3, flac, aac, opus and pcm16. Voice names remain model-specific strings.
+Omitted audio parameters remain omitted, allowing native vLLM-Omni defaults.
+Duplicate/unknown modalities and audio settings without an audio modality fail.
+
+An audio output request requires a model card declaring `audio_output`, plus
+all requested input capabilities. `audio_input` and `speech_generation` do not
+qualify a model for Chat audio output. Selection uses the ordinary recipe,
+candidate requirements and algorithm, including the single-candidate case.
+The selected model ID is re-encoded together with every mixed input block and
+output option. There is exactly one model inference request.
+
+Audio-bearing Chat responses use native same-protocol transport through Envoy:
+JSON audio data, transcript, ID, expiry, provider audio metadata, SSE frames and
+errors retain their original bytes. This also allows incremental delivery and
+client cancellation without an additional audio service or TTS call. Response
+conversion to Responses/Anthropic is deliberately rejected before selection;
+the standalone neutral response codec still rejects Chat audio objects. Native
+response bodies are not inspected by response-rewriting or response-cache
+plugins. Configure such policies only for interfaces on which they are supported.
+
+Source references: [Chat request API](https://developers.openai.com/api/reference/resources/chat)
+and the locked vLLM-Omni `entrypoints/openai/serving_chat.py` mixed-choice merge,
+`_resolve_audio_format`, and streaming audio metadata. Interface support is not
+evidence that a particular model can produce audio; model execution is a separate
+acceptance layer.
