+++ b/website/docs/api/native-images.md
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+title: Native image generation through ExtProc
+---
+
+`POST /v1/images/generations` accepts a JSON image-generation task. The prompt
+enters SR's neutral request representation, and typed generation options stay
+attached to that task. It does not call Chat Completions. Configure the backend
+with `api_format: images`, its actual provider model ID, and `text` plus
+`image_generation` model capabilities. A provider supporting the HTTP endpoint
+does not imply that its loaded model supports image generation.
+
+Direct image generation does not require the `tools` capability. Its distinct
+transport capability prevents conversion to another codec that would lose native
+diffusion controls. A plain chat request cannot select an images-only endpoint,
+including when it is the only candidate. The normal recipe, capability, context,
+and public entrypoint requirements apply before selection.
+
+The codec preserves `prompt`, `n`, `size`, `response_format`, `quality`, `user`,
+background, moderation, output format/compression, and the typed native fields in
+`pkg/llmprotocol/image_generation.go`. These include steps, seed, guidance,
+negative/system prompts, LoRA, VAE options, and bounded `extra_params`. Unknown
+fields, duplicate JSON keys, and invalid parameter values fail at ingress.
+The router does not invent a size or a text output-token budget for a native
+image request. `context: known_limits` still enforces the model's prompt bound.
+Model-specific value constraints remain the backend's responsibility.
+
+Same-wire responses preserve status, Content-Type, body chunks, URL responses,
+file responses, and backend errors. The router neither fetches returned URLs nor
+rewrites image bytes. URL/file responses cannot be converted to Responses or
+Chat; only the existing hosted b64 conversion is supported. Native streaming
+image generation and image edits are separate contracts, not implied by this
+endpoint. The downstream release records actual unit and gateway acceptance.
diff --git a/website/docs/api/native-mlx-video.md b/website/docs/api/native-mlx-video.md
